This code defines two classes, `Pdb` and `Pdbpp`, which are drop-in replacements for the built-in `pdb` and `pdbpp` modules. The `Pdb` class provides the basic functionality of `pdb`, while the `Pdbpp` class adds additional features such as improved performance, better support for multithreading, and easier integration with other tools and libraries.

The `Pdb` class uses a `ThreadSafeDict` to store the commands and their corresponding functions. The `Pdbpp` class uses a `ThreadSafeDict` to store the commands and their corresponding functions, and also adds additional methods such as `add_command`, `run_command`, `list_commands`, and `help_command`.

The example usage shows how to create an instance of `Pdbpp`, start it, set the current frame, add commands, run commands, get the stack trace, and run a function in a separate thread.

